-- title:
--   Gauss and σ-twisted readings give the same Igusa place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ over $k$ into the base change along $A \to k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) (the pushout of the finite and infinite chart spectra, for the chart algebras of elements integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j^{-1}]$), whose images together cover that base change; assume $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ is reduced with cardinality $n > 0$, and `modelTo` proper. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $k$ (a weight-one form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with integral $q$-expansion power series whose Laurent image over $k$ is nonzero), and let $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ be curve models over $k$ of the Igusa field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$, $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms. The reading hypotheses $\mathrm{hgauss}_1$, $\mathrm{hgauss}_2$ say: for $a$ in the finite chart algebra and power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \neq 0$ in $k$, if $a\,y = x$ (respectively $\sigma(a)\,y = x$) in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, then the element of the Igusa field obtained by pulling $a$ back along $e_i$ followed by $i_i$ followed by the first projection, restricting to the preimage of the finite chart, taking the germ at the generic point and transporting through $\mathrm{Mdl}_i.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, has Laurent expansion $\bar x/\bar y$; the corresponding preimage opens are assumed nonempty. Here $\sigma$ is an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with $\sigma j$ the $p$-fold $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), preserving the finite chart algebra, and such that every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ consisting exactly of the $f$ admitting a presentation $f\,y = x$ with $x, y$ power series over $A$, $\bar y \neq 0$, satisfies: the comap of $W_0$ along $\sigma$ differs from $W_0$, and contains both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ of nonzero reduction. Finally $\rho_\sigma$ is a ring automorphism of the finite chart algebra agreeing with $\sigma$. The conclusion: for every ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the finite chart algebra to $k$ that is $A$-linear, every $k$-point $c$ of $C_2$ whose composite into the two-chart model factors as $\operatorname{Spec}\chi$ followed by the finite-chart immersion [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231), and every $k$-point $c'$ of $C_1$ whose composite factors likewise through $\operatorname{Spec}(\chi \circ \rho_\sigma^{-1})$, the places of the Igusa function field attached by $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ to $c$ followed by $e_2^{-1}$ and by $\mathrm{Mdl}_1.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ to $c'$ followed by $e_1^{-1}$ coincide.
--
--   This transports reading data between the two components of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$: the untwisted (Gauss) reading on $C_1$ and the $\sigma$-twisted reading on $C_2$ assign one and the same place of the Igusa function field to points of the two components lying over $\sigma$-corresponding characters of the finite chart algebra. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.red_eq_red_smul_of_reducesSnd_of_gaussReading_snd_algEquiv_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.red_eq_red_smul_of_reducesSnd_of_gaussReading_snd_algEquiv_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and relies on the valuation-subring pair produced by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_pair_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_pair_x1_mul) together with the recognition criterion [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.eq_pointEquivPlace_of_forall_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits_of_isClosedImmersion`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel.eq_pointEquivPlace_of_forall_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_sub_algebraMap_mem_nonunits_of_isClosedImmersion).
